{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794250610652,"sessionID":"ses_e3e5da054ffe09B1wbTSsoF3hw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01JJoD1vZTHGNNA3w7jLyZPP","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && sed -i '1,/^--trusted-host/d' backend/requirements.lock && sed -i '/^$/{N;/^\\n$/D}' backend/requirements.lock; head -3 backend/requirements.lock; grep -c \"172.30\" frontend/package-lock.json; git show HEAD:frontend/package-lock.json | grep -c resolved; grep -m2 resolved frontend/package-lock.json; .venv/bin/pip install -q --timeout 120 -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -3","timeout":300000},"output":"\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d145f5445bf \\\n0\n44\n      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/@jridgewell/gen-mapping/-/gen-mapping-0.3.13.tgz\",\n      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/@jridgewell/remapping/-/remapping-2.3.5.tgz\",\nERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n","metadata":{"output":"\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d145f5445bf \\\n0\n44\n      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/@jridgewell/gen-mapping/-/gen-mapping-0.3.13.tgz\",\n      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/@jridgewell/remapping/-/remapping-2.3.5.tgz\",\nERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually